% The Vinberg diagram of (10,10,0)_1 = E_10(2): ten roots of square -4 (black)
% forming T_{2,3,7} = E_10, in Bourbaki's numbering.
% Computed: the output of Vinberg's algorithm on the lattice of the
% 2-elementary table in the research preamble
% (dzack_research.preamble.catalogue._TWO_ELEMENTARY_RECIPES), run with the
% engine the preamble registers for "vinberg_root_enumeration" (vinal,
% Bogachev-Perepechko); the search completed. Edge weights are read from the
% root Gram matrix, cos(pi/m) = |h_i.h_j| / sqrt(h_i^2 h_j^2), and the maximal
% parabolic subdiagrams are all vertex sets on which minus the Gram matrix is
% positive semidefinite with one kernel direction per component and rank
% rk(L) - 2.
% Maximal parabolic subdiagrams (`maximal parabolic=<name>`): one,
% E8 = E~_8 = {1..9}.
% Roots -1..-10, labelled by their index.
\coxeterlabels{index}
\coxeterEdiagram{10}{black}
\coxeterparabolic{E8}{{1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9},{2,4}}
